{"seq":16,"at":"2026-11-06T11:35:48.206Z","type":"report.text","job":"A","data":{"step":"search-1","provider":"search","text":"Cold-chain spoilage for regional grocers usually comes down to three levers: equipment and monitoring (refrigeration units, IoT temperature sensors, alarms), process and logistics (receiving checks, loading practices, rotation and shelf-life management), and supplier or transport arrangements (carrier contracts, reefer fleet ownership versus third-party logistics). A useful comparison should weigh upfront cost, payback period, spoilage reduction evidence, and how well each approach fits a grocer's scale and existing infrastructure. Any figures on spoilage rates or savings you find should be checked against their original source, since vendor-reported results and academic studies often differ in method and baseline."},"prev":"2e848c6a61f681c117f691d2d82fd0a10c927c85ae168f051fdb4587cd8a2bf6","hash":"1bbd86cbb5faf6f98f2c0410da0ac35d8470b7e715dd23a96adfa4c494fee5bf"}
{"seq":17,"at":"2026-11-06T11:36:03.280Z","type":"payment","job":"A","data":{"provider":"lookup","step":"lookup-1","price":"0.030000","spent":"0.070000","status":200,"tries":3,"ms":15071,"invoice":"0xcca0335af2e5c85d02d49cb7dbdce0e5a3aa664a0f326135ccd10b81290195b3:c895bb05-a052-43ca-b983-5d53eb62e664"},"prev":"1bbd86cbb5faf6f98f2c0410da0ac35d8470b7e715dd23a96adfa4c494fee5bf","hash":"7c80a6a75ef251140d619f4df49b084f59ded8df826a1d92d47666a72d63ac23"}
{"seq":18,"at":"2026-11-06T11:36:03.281Z","type":"report.text","job":"A","data":{"step":"lookup-1","provider":"lookup","text":"Note: I can't pull live data, so these notes cover what matters and what to verify, not retrieved figures. The three approaches (for example, passive insulated packaging, active refrigeration upgrades, and real-time temperature monitoring with alerts) should be compared on spoilage reduction, upfront and running cost, and fit with regional delivery distances. Check any spoilage rates or savings claims against the original studies or vendor data, and confirm which figures are from the grocers' own records versus marketing material."},"prev":"7c80a6a75ef251140d619f4df49b084f59ded8df826a1d92d47666a72d63ac23","hash":"7796e1efe24c36a72d5c653e9bee42c9276121a9baf7bd6d9247d4dbdef6388c"}
{"seq":19,"at":"2026-11-06T11:36:05.756Z","type":"step.upgraded","job":"A","data":{"paragraph":1,"provider":"model-premium","reason":"Opening paragraph: it frames the comparison of the three spoilage-reduction approaches, and readers rely on it most."},"prev":"7796e1efe24c36a72d5c653e9bee42c9276121a9baf7bd6d9247d4dbdef6388c","hash":"de84d558d12f40dd8fc9b6efac72829736761afaafbf0f0586fc61ff89e0fbc9"}
{"seq":20,"at":"2026-11-06T11:36:14.340Z","type":"payment","job":"A","data":{"provider":"model-premium","step":"model-1","price":"0.050000","spent":"0.120000","status":200,"tries":1,"ms":8581,"invoice":"0x301f3318d206687310ab56681eb8ba42e7841a798a13c75f41412c583570e42c:c4f4cc8b-178a-40e4-895c-5ac29d64ad0a"},"prev":"de84d558d12f40dd8fc9b6efac72829736761afaafbf0f0586fc61ff89e0fbc9","hash":"d8a6ff6b92b2c301f898df56a15b7502c8291a6a92db62931cfd0b0312097ce7"}
{"seq":21,"at":"2026-11-06T11:36:14.341Z","type":"report.text","job":"A","data":{"step":"model-1","provider":"model-premium","text":"This report compares three ways regional grocers can reduce cold-chain spoilage: investing in refrigeration equipment and continuous temperature monitoring, tightening handling processes from receiving dock to shelf, and restructuring transport through carrier contracts or owned reefer fleets. The choice matters because perishables carry thin margins, and every discarded case of dairy, produce, or meat erodes profit, strains supplier relationships, and adds disposal costs that smaller chains feel more sharply than national competitors."},"prev":"d8a6ff6b92b2c301f898df56a15b7502c8291a6a92db62931cfd0b0312097ce7","hash":"b0f4e5132e2d24d794b46a0f8971d62c9442712484723ba0f1c71af0d48aa04f"}
{"seq":22,"at":"2026-11-06T11:36:14.342Z","type":"step.upgraded","job":"A","data":{"paragraph":2,"provider":"model-premium","reason":"Probably the core comparison of the three approaches, where precise reasoning about tradeoffs matters most."},"prev":"b0f4e5132e2d24d794b46a0f8971d62c9442712484723ba0f1c71af0d48aa04f","hash":"5500489aa0d5e6fa8b3326b69a2add6d5300107bdaf5cbfe5274734f6422e19a"}
{"seq":23,"at":"2026-11-06T11:36:22.651Z","type":"payment","job":"A","data":{"provider":"model-premium","step":"model-2","price":"0.050000","spent":"0.170000","status":200,"tries":1,"ms":8307,"invoice":"0xbc29479cc526de3b75bbab7cad51c7eabc08256bff8c655edb5aaa3abb175198:ddf5d271-62b0-478f-9f0d-330de7c52509"},"prev":"5500489aa0d5e6fa8b3326b69a2add6d5300107bdaf5cbfe5274734f6422e19a","hash":"260e54e73ae97f8ab9e35fbe2fcf5073fd386395a7c10979b4a1128d1485e963"}
{"seq":24,"at":"2026-11-06T11:36:22.652Z","type":"report.text","job":"A","data":{"step":"model-2","provider":"model-premium","text":"Equipment and monitoring is usually the most capital-intensive option, but also the easiest to measure. Wireless sensors in walk-in coolers, display cases, and delivery trailers log temperatures continuously and alert staff when readings drift, so product can be moved before it spoils rather than written off at closing. To judge payback, compare shrink logs for monitored and unmonitored units over several months, tracking excursion frequency, response time, and the value of product saved."},"prev":"260e54e73ae97f8ab9e35fbe2fcf5073fd386395a7c10979b4a1128d1485e963","hash":"16d27154178eecfb4f9077cfbf168ce229acefce45d781eb3dfa75415902dda8"}
{"seq":25,"at":"2026-11-06T11:36:22.653Z","type":"step.upgraded","job":"A","data":{"paragraph":3,"provider":"model-premium","reason":"Likely the conclusion or recommendation that grocers will act on, so accuracy is worth the cost."},"prev":"16d27154178eecfb4f9077cfbf168ce229acefce45d781eb3dfa75415902dda8","hash":"2b6d74e4491124c06b65eaf2871d6bc64357d11793c513721477ba75d2155eba"}
{"seq":26,"at":"2026-11-06T11:36:29.288Z","type":"payment","job":"A","data":{"provider":"model-premium","step":"model-3","price":"0.050000","spent":"0.220000","status":200,"tries":1,"ms":6633,"invoice":"0xc69391f8d9f9ead6e13f38f41155f788d3ea052738e31e7a5d06fec5dda3e9e7:361bc839-926b-476e-936e-1122958d8b54"},"prev":"2b6d74e4491124c06b65eaf2871d6bc64357d11793c513721477ba75d2155eba","hash":"af2e3641fb641a07b6a24135938ef9519619fe9fc8996eb7e2693de93c91a469"}
{"seq":27,"at":"2026-11-06T11:36:29.289Z","type":"report.text","job":"A","data":{"step":"model-3","provider":"model-premium","text":"Process discipline and transport restructuring complete the picture. Tighter receiving checks, first-expired-first-out rotation, and limits on dock dwell time cost little but depend on staff consistency, while renegotiated carrier terms or owned reefers suit chains with long rural routes. For most regional grocers, the practical sequence is to start with process fixes, add monitoring where shrink logs show the heaviest losses, and revisit transport only once those gains are measured."},"prev":"af2e3641fb641a07b6a24135938ef9519619fe9fc8996eb7e2693de93c91a469","hash":"78da72b3562a0995a4cdcf273aaaa4d19b015ca7605014250b61c96b54c406de"}
